cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies."
title: "Braess Lab"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, client-only web application that serves as the interactive
  computational companion to the paper "Braess' Paradox in Uniform Affine Grid
  Networks" by Andy Lu and Steven J. Miller. It re-solves the user equilibrium
  of uniform affine grids plus one chord in real time using the paper's
  closed-form spectral machinery, reproduces the paper's published results as
  validated test fixtures, and runs a Web Worker search for the chord placement
  that maximizes the Braess Ratio.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Andy
  - family-names: Miller
    given-names: "Steven J."
repository-code: "https://github.com/anlu9183/braess-lab"
url: "https://github.com/anlu9183/braess-lab"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"
keywords:
  - "Braess' paradox"
  - "selfish routing"
  - "user equilibrium"
  - "traffic networks"
  - "spectral graph theory"
  - "Laplacian pseudoinverse"
